cmark-gfm
------------------------------------------
cmark-gfm is an extended version of the C reference implementation of
CommonMark, a rationalized version of Markdown syntax with a spec.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libcmark-gfm-devel-0.29.0.gfm.13-1bl2
  libcmark-gfm0.29.0.gfm.13-0.29.0.gfm.13-1bl2
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/github/cmark-gfm

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/github/cmark-gfm/archive/refs/tags/0.29.0.gfm.13.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack cmark-gfm-0.29.0.gfm.13-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./cmark-gfm-0.29.0.gfm.13-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/cmark-gfm-0.29.0.gfm.13-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/cmark-gfm-0.29.0.gfm.13-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcmark-gfm0.29.0.gfm.13-0.29.0.gfm.13-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcmark-gfm-devel-0.29.0.gfm.13-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(cmark-gfm)
  /usr/bin/cmark-gfm.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/cmark-gfm.README
  /usr/share/doc/cmark-gfm/COPYING
  /usr/share/doc/cmark-gfm/README.md
  /usr/share/man/man1/cmark-gfm.1.gz
  /usr/share/man/man3/cmark-gfm.3.gz

(libcmark-gfm0.29.0.gfm.13)
  /usr/bin/cygcmark-gfm-0.29.0.gfm.13.dll
  /usr/bin/cygcmark-gfm-extensions-0.29.0.gfm.13.dll

(libcmark-gfm-devel)
  /usr/include/cmark-gfm-core-extensions.h
  /usr/include/cmark-gfm-extension_api.h
  /usr/include/cmark-gfm.h
  /usr/include/cmark-gfm_export.h
  /usr/include/cmark-gfm_version.h
  /usr/lib/cmake/cmake-gfm-extensions/cmark-gfm-extensions-relwithdebinfo.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/cmake-gfm-extensions/cmark-gfm-extensions.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/cmake-gfm/cmark-gfm-relwithdebinfo.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/cmake-gfm/cmark-gfm.cmake
  /usr/lib/libcmark-gfm-extensions.dll.a
  /usr/lib/libcmark-gfm.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/libcmark-gfm.pc

